   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the insurance law, in relation to imposing standards for\ncertain examination services",
    "basePrintNo": "S9832",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S9832-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §2103, Ins L",
    "lawSection": "Insurance Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S9832\n\nSPONSOR: BAILEY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the insurance law, in relation to imposing standards for\ncertain examination services\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to codify existing Department of Financial\nServices standards for producer exam test vendors.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends paragraph 1 of subdivision f of section 2103 of the\ninsurance law by adding a new subparagraph to require that vendors score\nproducer licensing examinations in accordance with Department of Finan-\ncial Services contractual practices and the National Association of\nInsurance Commissioner (NAIC) standards.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe National Association of Insurance Commissioner (NAIC) has developed\nboth standards and best practices for licensing producer exam develop-\nment, scoring, and administration. These standards serve the interest of\nconsumers, regulators, industry and prospective insurance producers. The\nDepartment of Financial Services has adopted these standards for its\ncurrent examination vendor. This bill would codify this practice subject\nto revision by the Superintendent by regulation.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately\n",
    "multiSponsors": {
